  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "tcp: Send the header to the tap even with exceptions in options",
  "description": "The TCP tap sends the header information to its listeners, most of\nwhich only need the information in the beginning of the fixed header.\nIt doesn't get sent until after parsing the TCP options, in order\nto add information about SACKs (which most taps don't need, but\nat least the TCP stream graph can take advantage of if there.)\n\nAdd a cleanup function so that if we hit an exception while parsing\nthe options, we go ahead and send what we have in the header to the\ntaps.\n\nFix #18138.",
  "state": "merged",
